call me furina and im a student who likes to code and stuff,

## languages

recently ive taken a liking for C. either way, heres the languages that i like
and use constantly:

- c99: the bestest language ever
- [zig](https://ziglang.org/): i really love where theyre going with this
- [golang](https://go.dev/): convenient for big projects, has its drawbacks
- posix shell: the one to join them all

and heres some more that i have adequate experience with:

- [rust](https://rust-lang.org/): its fast, and if you like pain its also safe
- [python3](https://python.org/): i just used it for 3 whole years straight im
  good at it i think

and some miscancellous generic stuff like:

- generic webdev stuff like html/css/js
- better webdev stuff like ts/scss/[tailwind](https://tailwindcss.com/)
- frameworks like [svelte](https://svelte.dev/)
  (+[sveltekit](https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/introduction)),
  [solidjs](https://solidjs.org/), and [astro](https://astro.build/)

## cool projects

- [pebl](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/pebl/): a tiny kernel in C for
  [RISC-V architecture](https://riscv.org/) (cross-arch support soon?)
- [envidiyuh](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/envidiyuh): a fast runtime for
(byte-level) [markov chains](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markov_chain)
- [lexyc](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/lexyc/): x86(64) compiler for a
  turing-complete esoteric programming language in zig
  ([see original](https://git.gay/noraaoki/xy))
- [brainfucc](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/brainfucc/): a brainfuck compiler
in C targeting the greatest architecture: RISC-V

### miscancellous projects

- [ziggymirror](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/ziggymirror/): a
  [community mirror](https://ziglang.org/news/announcing-community-mirrors/)
  for downloading zig written in posix shell
- [yurisync](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/yurisync/): a generic bluesky media
  sync tool that i branded with yuri because yuri is very important
- [gopresence](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/gopresence/): discord presence
  library for golang programs (cross platform, and doesnt suck)

## interests

eh its more like i randomly start doing stuff but generally most
of my likings can be classified into:

- networking: anything that involves two devices communicating
- graphics: started learning opengl and its awesome
- osdev: recently dipped my pinky toe into this, and let me tell you, its
  awesome. you should really try it out
- creatures of steel

### setup

i main [void linux](https://voidlinux.org/) and i love it. i
use the [niri](https://niri-wm.github.io/niri/) window manager, and primarily
[helix](http://helix-editor.com/) text editor/IDE.

i had a homelab setup on an old laptop but rn its offline. it would otherwise
be available with reasonable uptime on this domain, as well as on the alt url
https://focalors.pp.ua

